WEBVTT

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:36.050
When I open my photo book, I see different sides of me. {purichou...}

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.820
Laughing, {warattari}

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.600
or playing it cool, in all the pictures. {sumashitari de...}

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.330
I don't wanna say, "what's with all these characters?" But... {nani kore...}

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.040
Isn't this too much fun? {arisugi...}

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.620
For real? {maji...}

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.830
I mean, thanks! {tte yuu ka...}

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.160
Even if I lose my way,  {maigo ni...}

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.770
my heart's egg {kokoro no...}

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.540
will be all right. Come back {daijoubu...}

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.230
to me! {modotteoide}

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.010
Hey, when we're together... {kimi to...}

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.730
Hop, step, jump!

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.340
Because you're here... {kimi ga...}

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.990
Drew, draw, drawn!

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.860
I'm always with you...  {kimi to...}

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.580
Chip, syrup, whip!

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.260
One more time,  {mou ichido...}

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.870
unlock my heart! {kokoro...}

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.640
I love you.  {daisuki yo}

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.100
All of you.  {minna}

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.990
I want to be next to you. {soba ni...}

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.300
Okay? {ne...}

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.450
Love ya! {suki yo}

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.000
This manga is hilarious!

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.210
You could call it art!

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.610
For real!

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.220
Shut up!

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.170
We're in the middle of a meeting.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.200
Be quiet.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.180
How extremely rude.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.100
We're sorry.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.670
Well, we've decided to transplant the flower garden,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.720
so that'll be all for today.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.140
I'll need to buy equipment tomorrow,

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.940
so we won't hold a Guardians' meeting.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:19.690
Yay!

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:20.740
No meeting!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.220
Sheesh, Yaya.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.560
That's what you say,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.890
but you're really excited on the inside, right?

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.490
Since you'll be all alone with Tadase when you two go shopping tomorrow.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.760
I-I'm not excited or anything.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.210
Yaya, this manga rules!

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.770
Doesn't it?

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.390
It's such a riot!

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.340
Man, that's brilliant!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.830
Oh, a gag manga, I see.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.440
Ah, I know this one.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.640
It's really popular.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.270
<i>Gag Manga Daioh.</i>

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.430
This balancing gag is great.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.750
Balance-chu!

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.770
You mean Bala-Balance.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.420
Huh?

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.270
You know it, Rima-tan?

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.850
N-Not really.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.560
Oh.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.820
Huh? Are you texting a servant?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.720
No. My mother.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.520
The meeting ended early,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.560
so I have to let her know that I need to be picked up sooner.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:10.490
Picked up?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.680
Is Rima-tan a rich girl?

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:13.910
Not really.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:14.930
I'm normal.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.300
So long, then.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.020
See ya later!

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:18.780
Ah.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.520
If you've never read this before, do you want to borrow it?

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.620
<i>Gag Manga Daioh.</i>

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.870
It's so funny!

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.220
They pose like this and go...

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.770
Balance!

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.310
It's Bala-Balance!

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.270
What's with her?

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.540
Boy, that was a surprise.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.970
Yeah.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.190
That was close. So close.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:57.050
You almost Character Changed.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:02.850
The Lonesome Queen!

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:02.850
Episode 32

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:04.700
6th Grade Star Class

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.640
Pipe down!

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.020
Jeez. Quiet down, everyone!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.190
Sure is lively in here.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:16.240
Nikaidou-sensei's on a business trip, so he's away today.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.810
Huh? What?

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.810
I can't stand this chaotic atmosphere.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.470
We should Character Change and lay down the law!

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.680
Citizens!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.100
Idle chatter is forbidden in the presence of the King!

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.890
Grovel at my feet!

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.900
No, that'd be a little...

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.790
Jeez.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.530
We can't hold a class meeting like this.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.610
Class rep!

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:40.350
What is it?

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.040
The boys in front are blocking our view of the blackboard!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.650
Hello, are you people listening?

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:47.960
There's nothing you can do.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.170
My desk is in the front.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.310
It's as the Queen says!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.140
This is really aggravating me!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:55.970
Don't...

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:56.920
Be rude...

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:57.770
To Rima-sama!

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.500
Don't give in, Yamabuki-san!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.730
Let's show them what we're made of!

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.640
Ah, this is the first time I've ever experienced such unity!

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.550
What a gigantic mess.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.620
I'm amazed they don't get tired of it.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.890
Amu-chan, you've gotta do something.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.850
This is all...

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.650
All because I'm...

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.550
You guys should back down!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.350
Not a chance!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:40.220
Class Meeting

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.550
If you can't see 'cause they're blocking the front, just turn around.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.960
Okay, all yours.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.220
Thank you, Hinamori-san!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.500
That's our Amu-chan!

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.420
Ready and...

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.430
"Cool & spicy!"

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.560
Ah, I was so nervous!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.890
All right, let's give the class meeting another shot.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:05.020
We've acquired a lot of books recently, and the shelf's become a mess.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:11.010
So, I'd like to appoint a bookshelf monitor to tidy it up once a week.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.270
Huh?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.420
Okay, everyone.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.390
Please draw one lot each.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.390
Miss.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.900
I drew a miss.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.860
Miss.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.470
Ah, what a relief!

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.160
Hit

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.990
Rima-sama drew a hit!

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.890
Oh that poor thing.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:31.080
Work hard!

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.150
Good thing it wasn't me.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.360
But I

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.910
can't go home too late.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.780
The Guardians don't have anything up today, right?

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.380
The class decided on this, so you have to follow it.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.580
She looks troubled.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.970
Is she okay?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.740
Work hard then, Mashiro-san.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.770
I'd love to help, but I have club activities.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:57.660
Sorry!

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.390
I have cram school.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.390
Bye-bye!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.740
Rima-sama, I'm sorry.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.390
We're counting on you, Mashiro-san.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.550
Rima-sama, I have to go now.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.720
Let's go, Hinamori-san.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.800
This is today's shopping list.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.560
Thanks.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.340
A shopping date.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.310
Doesn't that sound wonderful?

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:20.990
Uh-huh.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:23.060
Bala-Balance!

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.560
Bala-Balance!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.730
Is something wrong?

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.670
I'm gonna help, too!

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.310
Sorry, Rima.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.540
This won't work, Rima.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.390
There are times when you get out late, and times when you're early.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.220
Honestly, why did you join this weird Guardian club?

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.250
But Mom...

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:13.690
This is why I wish you'd go to a school closer to home.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.890
But your father always decides everything without me.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.660
In fact, just the other day...

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:21.830
That man is always so...

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.130
Rima.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.020
Rima!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.470
Look, look!

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.120
Funny face!

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:33.930
Ouch.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.180
I screwed up!

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.820
She smiled!

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.620
Rima smiled!

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.310
I'll take care of the two upper shelves,

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.210
so you're responsible for the lower ones.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.680
Let's get this over with.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.320
We're helping, too!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.180
Let's clean this up quickly, and get home!

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.200
I'm helping, too!

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:02.830
Why?

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.150
Why what?

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.320
I didn't ask for your help.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.890
Nobody asked me to help.

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:07.710
Here.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:08.820
Busybody.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.220
You're pretty stubborn yourself, Mashiro-san.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:14.920
Rima.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:15.640
Huh?

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.350
Call me Rima.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.100
Then call me Amu.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.940
They're both stubborn.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:26.650
For real.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.330
They're pretty similar.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:37.270
Jeez, who brought manga?

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:38.900
Ah, this is...

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.620
Isn't this the one you guys were reading yesterday?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.630
No.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.310
That's the fourth volume that was just released!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:46.380
Huh?

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:47.830
They were reading the third volume yesterday.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:48.770
Give me that!

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.930
Could this be...

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.350
Rima, let's do the usual!

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.640
Bala-Balance!

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.190
Bala-Balance!

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.960
Bala-Balance!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.040
Is that...

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.470
A Character Change?

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:13.640
Is it?

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.420
U-Um...

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.430
She turned into a ball?

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:26.800
Rima, do you...

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.640
Do you happen to love gags?

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.600
Got a problem with that?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.950
Yes, and I'm really particular about comedy!

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.640
I can't forgive people who don't take gags seriously!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.140
What of it?!

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.680
I can't tell if she's snapping at me or bragging.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.180
That's a crazy gap.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.510
So that's why you kept your Character Change a secret?

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.640
No!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.000
There's no need to hide it.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.680
No! It's not cool!

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:52.040
You absolutely cannot tell <i>anyone!</i>

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:01.180
Rima might actually be pretty cute.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.170
The story continues to unfold.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:12.020
The Queen and Joker are growing closer.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:13.770
All that remains is...

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:16.790
Ah, the Jack?

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.330
The Guardians are on a break.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.390
It's a perfect opportunity for covert activities.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.950
Though, as a warrior, I feel reluctant carrying out this task.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:52.420
I believe this is the data concerning all X Egg hunting carried out by the Guardians.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.720
The Joker: Hinamori Amu.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:59.200
When she performs a Character Transformation with the Guardian Character Ran,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.830
she becomes Amulet Heart.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:04.970
She uses the power of the Humpty Lock to invoke Open Heart,

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.430
and cleanses X Eggs.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.850
The Character Transformation with Miki leads to Amulet Spade.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.600
With Su, it's Amulet Clover.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:20.810
It would appear she is indeed the only one who can cleanse X Eggs.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.340
Hinamori Amu.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:28.770
Sister.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.970
Well? Making any progress with your spying?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.120
If you uncover any secrets, let me know immediately.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.310
Especially regarding Hinamori Amu.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.400
I get the feeling she's the key.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.320
Make sure you conduct a thorough investigation.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.170
Yes, Sister.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.560
That should do it.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.210
A tidy shelf brings a sparkling smile to your face.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.220
Yep.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:02.110
All right, let's go home.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:02.980
Okay.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:04.430
Oh no!

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.680
I forgot to call my mom!

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.950
Is your mother picking you up?

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:11.850
Yeah.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.850
I have to go!

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:18.100
Bye, Amu.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:26.240
That was the first time Rima called you Amu.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:26.850
Yep.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.540
It's kind of weird, though.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.870
If her parents are nice enough to pick her up,

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.720
are they going to be that mad if she's a little late?

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:37.290
She must be a punctual Type A sort of person.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.350
Just like me.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:40.240
You're Type A?

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:43.020
So we actually have blood types...

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.240
Chairman.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.180
Joker.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.640
Why are you here so late?

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.680
I was looking something up.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.570
Anyway, why do you call me "Chairman?"

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.810
Well, you just seem like the Chairman type.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:01.640
We can't admit that we were looking for the Guardians' weaknesses.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:02.280
Musashi.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.740
Oh, that's right.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.390
You've got a bunch of data, right?

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:08.300
Uh, y-yeah.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.850
Do you know anything about Rima?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.630
Why does she have to be picked up?

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:13.680
U-Uh...

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.430
I don't know the specifics,

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.140
but the Queen was almost kidnapped at one point.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.760
Kidnapped?

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.240
It was only an attempt, however,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.140
and she returned soon after as though nothing had happened.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:31.390
It may have some relation as to why her parents pick her up.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.990
Really.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:37.830
However, the school and her parents have been arguing over who bears responsibility for it,

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:41.400
and it's been going on for a while.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:45.790
Rima.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.100
I wonder how she feels.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.810
If it were me...

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.320
Didn't I tell you?

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:59.310
I have a job, too!

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:02.720
How hard do you think it is to slip away from work to pick her up?

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.300
Yet you keep forcing me to do it every day.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.590
Do you realize that you're her father?

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.200
Hello?

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.440
Honestly.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.330
Hello, everyone.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.020
Good morning!

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:41.210
Before I start taking attendance,

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.700
direct your attention thataway!

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.760
It's really tidy!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.680
Mashiro-san did a great job!

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.770
What a surprise.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.270
That's our Rima-sama!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.390
Now, back to taking attendance-

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.660
And just like that, school's out!

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.370
Huh?!

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.460
Rima-sama,

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.750
forgive my behavior yesterday!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:06.970
Rima-sama, allow me to carry your belongings!

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.530
Rima-sama, here's a towel.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:08.990
Rima.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:09.810
Let's go!

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:10.970
Ready and...

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.470
Bala-Balance!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.770
Your pose is all wrong!

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.350
Huh? Was it like this?

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:17.340
Wasn't it like this?

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.290
That's wrong!

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:20.330
It should be like this.

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.520
That's the one you like, right?

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:25.800
Huh?

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.170
What was that?

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.740
It's all wrong!

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.010
Wait! Calm down!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.120
They're just playing around!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:32.820
Comedy...

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.760
Gags are no laughing matter!

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.020
A Character Change out of nowhere?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.230
Rima, the usual!

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.240
Wait, Rima!

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:39.280
Let's go!

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:40.560
C-Calm down.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:40.560
Ready and...

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.600
Bala-Balance!

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.130
Bala-Balance!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.890
Bala-Balance!

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:54.540
Bala-Balance!

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:55.500
Uh...

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.930
R-Rima-sama?

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.340
R-Rima.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.640
Um...

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.150
That was awesome!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.880
The actions were perfect!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.350
Her character's totally different!

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.930
N-No way!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.520
Our Rima-sama is...

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.430
Rima, wait!

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.840
That was great!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.500
The lofty Rima-sama...

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:29.090
It can't be true! Tell me this isn't true!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:31.410
That wasn't Rima-sama!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:32.890
It <i>was</i> her.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.770
That was Rima, too.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:41.900
Amu-chan.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.130
Rima!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.520
Rima!

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.310
Rima!

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.350
Where did she go?

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.890
Amu-chan!

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.460
Over here!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:01.880
A ball?

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.560
You think this serves me right.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:22.570
Why would I?

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.020
Girls never like me.

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.670
That's not true.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.200
Well, maybe a little.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.520
Um...

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.020
I've screwed up before.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:34.770
Yes!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:37.770
I like you, Prince!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.560
I Character Changed and went crazy in front of everyone.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.250
It was so completely lame,

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.970
but it ended up being pretty well-received.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.510
It was a relief, in a way.

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.800
It's pretty tiring to use your outside character all the time.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.090
I like comedy.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:52.220
Gags, too.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:56.220
But I hate the fact that I can't make anyone else laugh.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:01.620
When I was little, I would joke around and make everyone laugh.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.680
I was happy when my mom and dad laughed.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.680
But eventually I realized...

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:10.280
That laughing is stupid.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:12.100
It's useless.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:16.930
Childish and weak people use humor only as an escape mechanism.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:20.130
A lame joke just leaves you feeling cold, right?

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.310
Nobody needs that.

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:31.570
The other day,

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:35.750
you told me that I just have to take back my X Egg.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.470
That made me happy.

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:43.710
Because it meant that Dia isn't an unnecessary character.

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:46.190
She's part of the real me, too.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.100
Let's go, Rima.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.450
Let's get your bag from the classroom and go home.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.440
Your dad's coming to pick you up, right?

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:03.810
Let go, Rima.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.290
Don't pull like that.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:06.960
You'll stretch my uniform.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:07.810
Uh-huh.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.310
Yeah, I just said...

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.050
They're all buddy-buddy now.

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.890
They're getting along nicely.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.550
Getting along!

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:18.100
Man, what a huge shock.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.570
I didn't expect Rima-sama to be a gag character like that.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.100
What a letdown.

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.660
Second Cute Girl Ranking

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.640
This'll definitely shake up the rankings.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:27.020
They don't know when to stop.

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:29.400
Okay, I'll announce the results!

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.020
Crap! Hide it!

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:45.430
Let's go, Rima.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.260
Wh-What just happened?

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.920
We didn't do anything...

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.850
Right?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.180
Wanna go home?

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.470
Did you see their faces?

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:03.600
Sure did!

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:04.970
You rule, Amu-chan!

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.100
See you, Rima!

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:16.050
Bye-bye!

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:17.650
See ya later!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:29.110
Dad, I'm sorry you had to wait.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.210
Rima.

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:48.660
Rima!

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:50.740
Look! Look!

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:52.660
Funny face, part two!

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.570
See? See?

00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:57.650
Isn't it hilarious?

00:21:59.890 --> 00:22:01.970
Come on, smile.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:06.270
Rima!

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:10.450
Hey, Rima,

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:13.010
can you see the stars?

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:14.900
Yeah.

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:40.630
You can't think that there's {kotaenante...}

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:44.010
an answer out there somewhere, you see. {arutte...}

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:50.310
Because the only place you'll find it is inside you. {kotaenante...}

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:52.550
Ain't that cool? {kakkoii...}

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:57.500
The fact is, all you're truly feeling... {arinomama...}

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.830
Yup, it's love! {yappa...}

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:05.390
And right now, all those feelings are welling up. {ima no mama...}

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:09.160
So head toward the sun, give it everything you've got. {sei ippai...}

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:12.770
Try bustin' through. {butsukete...}

00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:16.140
Face forward, raise your head up high. {maemuite...}

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.050
There's no time to cry. {naiteru...}

00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:23.300
A passionate kiss! This "youthful" kiss! {jounetsu...}

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:27.300
I love you when you're trying your best, like now.  {ima ganbatteru...}

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:30.550
The best kiss! This "all-out" kiss! {saiko no...}

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:34.530
I want to show you these feelings that fill my heart. {mune ippai...}

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:39.230
I L-O-V-E Y-O-U.

00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:48.360
{blaarg}I am number one today!

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:51.800
Ah, what am I going to do?

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.350
Tadase-kun asked me out on a date!

00:23:54.350 --> 00:23:57.310
It's just to make up for the shopping you were supposed to do today.

00:23:57.310 --> 00:23:59.420
You shouldn't try to show off.

00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:00.880
It's just for the preview.

00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:03.350
Ah, but I can't wait!

00:24:03.350 --> 00:24:05.480
I've heard every single word,

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:09.460
and I'll be reporting on this romantic event!

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:11.230
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:12.890
I Can't Help But Fall in Love!

00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:15.090
Love flags are popping up everywhere!

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.670
Only because Amu-chan's so fickle.

00:24:16.670 --> 00:24:18.170
That's not true!

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:19.640
Maybe.
